			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Eliminate binary module re-exports for explicit paths\n\nRemove all `pub use` re-exports from `Source/Binary/mod.rs`, including those for `Main`, `Build`, `Register`, `Service`, and `Initialize`. Replace the legacy import shortcuts with a comment directing developers to use the full reverse-hierarchical path (`Binary::Main::Entry::Fn`, `Binary::Build::LocalhostPlugin::Fn`, etc.).\n\nThis aligns the entry point with the project's strict `Struct::Struct` naming convention and the `Nameless Exports` policy documented in `.claude/Naming-Convention.md`. The change enforces explicit call paths, reducing module resolution ambiguity and preventing reliance on convenience exports during the ongoing architecture migration.",
			"SHA": "83278ec9e89b6661773208e5146d7bd03e109e4b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:37:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1128,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Align ApplicationState import paths to nested convention\n\nStandardize imports for `ApplicationState` and `MapLockError` in `Bootstrap.rs`, `SourceControlManagement.rs`, and `TreeView.rs` to use the explicit nested path `State::ApplicationState::ApplicationState`. This change enforces the project's strict `Struct::Struct` naming convention and resolves module resolution ambiguity observed in recent IPC refactoring.\n\nThe updates replace flattened import paths with the fully qualified `ApplicationState::State::ApplicationState` structure, ensuring consistency with the `Track` subsystem and other core modules. No functional logic is altered; this is a pure structural alignment to maintain codebase clarity during the ongoing architecture migration.",
			"SHA": "030d6dca5b2fa25467d592a128b0d883f7dee2c9"
